Engineering Understanding:

Is constructed from Engineering Evidence.
Supports Engineering Reasoning.
Produces Decision Support.
Is preserved by Engineering Memory.
Contributes to Engineering Knowledge through long-term validation.
6. Responsibilities

Engineering Understanding is responsible for:

Representing Engineering Reality.
Integrating Engineering Evidence.
Maintaining engineering context.
Supporting engineering reasoning.
Supporting engineering decisions.
Evolving as new evidence becomes available.
Providing a coherent engineering model.
7. Normative Requirements

Engineering Understanding SHALL:

Be constructed from Engineering Evidence.
Maintain explicit engineering context.
Support explainable engineering reasoning.
Preserve traceability to supporting evidence.
Evolve when Engineering Evidence changes.
Remain internally consistent.

Atlas SHALL NOT treat unsupported assumptions as Engineering Understanding.

8. Non-Goals

Engineering Understanding does not:

Replace Engineering Reality.
Replace Engineering Evidence.
Replace human engineering judgment.
Represent permanent Engineering Knowledge.
Represent archived Engineering Memory.
Prescribe engineering decisions.
9. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY extend the representation of Engineering Understanding with richer semantic models, confidence metrics, relationship models, and contextual structures, provided the canonical definition established by this specification remains unchanged.